  "worked_solution": "The elements of $A$ are all the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{n+4},\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nLet's write down the first few terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{1+4}=\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2+4}=\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{3+4}=\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ {a}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{4+4}=\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & \u22ee\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA={\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{1}{6},\\frac{1}{7},\\frac{1}{8},\u2026}.\n$$",
